# One SCA scanner, not four. grype, trivy and bearer each bring their own vulnerability database and
# their own walk of the tree, over the same pnpm lockfile that osv-scanner covers. A project that
# needs container or SBOM scanning enables the one that answers that question, in its own config,
# rather than paying for three in CI.
#
# osv-scanner is off here as well, for now. Until 2.6.0 it read only the first document of a pnpm 11+
# lockfile, pnpm's own packages, and passed by missing the rest; it now reports 43 known
# vulnerabilities in this repository's dependencies. See
# docs/backlog/dependencies-carry-known-vulnerabilities-with-osv-scanner-off.md.
**/*: grype, trivy, bearer, osv-scanner

# Generated layer→subtree maps (devtools dockerfile --emit-oci-map): raw
# generator output must stay byte-stable for the Dockerfile drift gate.
docker/oci-map*.json: *
